// Full render-hide invisibility has no primitive in this engine -- see
// Sequester's own doc comment ("functionally invisible, not a render-hide"):
// the detection-multiplier trick (BuffEffect::Stealth) is the only
// concealment mechanism that exists. Reuses PassWithoutTrace (a pure Stealth
// contribution, no other rider) rather than the heavier Sequester (which
// also bundles Nondetection and is calibrated for its own level-7 capstone,
// strength 20.0) -- this is a level-2 spell, calibrated instead against
// pass_without_trace.ron's own strength: 1.0 for its level-2 group aura,
// bumped up since this is a dedicated single-target SelfBuff rather than a
// shared aura. The source spell's "touch a creature" targeting narrows to
// self-only, the same Touch-range-SelfBuff narrowing nondetection.ron/
// sequester.ron/magic_aura.ron already document -- SelfBuff always lands on
// the caster (see common/src/states/self_buff.rs).
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.2,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(kind: PassWithoutTrace, data: BuffData(strength: 2.0, duration: Some(60.0))),
    ],
    energy_cost: 45.0,
    meta: (
        school: Some(Illusion),
        source: Some(Arcane),
        // level 2 spell -> min_level 12, the `level * 6` convention (see
        // sleep.ron).
        requirements: (min_level: Some(12)),
    ),
)
